<mxPoint x="0" y="0" as="offset"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e13" value="12" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2.5;strokeColor=#232F3E;dashed=1;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;labelBorderColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;fontColor=#232F3E;" edge="1" parent="1" source="alm1" target="sns1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e14" value="13" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2.5;strokeColor=#232F3E;dashed=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;labelBorderColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;fontColor=#232F3E;" edge="1" parent="1" source="sns1" target="email1"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="800" y="1670"/><mxPoint x="170" y="1670"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e15" value="14" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2.5;strokeColor=#232F3E;dashed=0;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;labelBorderColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;fontColor=#232F3E;" edge="1" parent="1" source="gh" target="cfn"><mxGeometry x="-0.3" relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="0" y="0" as="offset"/></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e16" value="15" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2.5;strokeColor=#232F3E;dashed=0;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;labelBorderColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;fontColor=#232F3E;" edge="1" parent="1" source="gh" target="art"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="170" y="2090"/><mxPoint x="2300" y="2090"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="e17" value="16" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;strokeWidth=2.5;strokeColor=#232F3E;dashed=0;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;labelBorderColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=1;fontSize=14;fontColor=#232F3E;" edge="1" parent="1" source="cli" target="cog"><mxGeometry x="0.2" relative="1" as="geometry"><mxPoint x="0" y="0" as="offset"/><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="320" y="1240"/><mxPoint x="320" y="1380"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="legend" value="Legend and notes" style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#f8fafc;strokeColor=#232F3E;strokeWidth=2;dashed=0;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=16;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#232F3E;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=8;spacingBottom=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="2150" width="2820" height="350" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="legL" value="&lt;b&gt;Requests&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;[1] Users open the page over HTTPS on the custom domain (TLS 1.2 or later; prod adds the shared WAF).&lt;br&gt;[2] Route 53 A and AAAA alias records point the domain at the distribution (dotted: DNS).&lt;br&gt;[3] CloudFront reads the private web bucket with origin access control (SigV4).&lt;br&gt;[4] CloudFront sends /auth/* (login, refresh, logout) to the BFF function URL, signed (OAC, AWS_IAM).&lt;br&gt;[5] The BFF reads the app client secret once per execution environment (secretsmanager:GetSecretValue).&lt;br&gt;[6] The BFF calls Cognito InitiateAuth, GetTokensFromRefreshToken and RevokeToken with the secret hash or secret (confidential client only).&lt;br&gt;[7] The page calls the backends directly with the ID token as bearer (dotted: other repositories).&lt;br&gt;[8] The us-east-1 certificate is attached to the distribution (passed to stack frontend by the deploy script).&lt;br&gt;[9] At deploy time the auth stack fills the secret from the app client attribute ClientSecret (dotted).&lt;br&gt;[16] The websocket CLI and e2e tests sign in directly at Cognito with the public client ID (USER_PASSWORD_AUTH, refresh, revoke; TLS, no BFF, no WAF, no secret), then call the websocket backend with the ID token. A public-client refresh token sent to the BFF /auth/refresh is refused by Cognito (different client)." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=15;fontColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=0;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="70" y="2200" width="1360" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="legR" value="&lt;b&gt;Alerts and delivery&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;[10] [11] BFF Errors and Throttles alarms notify the us-east-2 topic, which emails the owner.&lt;br&gt;[12] [13] Certificate expiry alarms (30 and 7 days) notify the us-east-1 topic, which emails the owner.&lt;br&gt;[14] GitHub Actions deploys the stacks in order auth, cert, auth-bff, frontend through guarded change sets, after the owner guard; IAC_TOOL=terraform runs Terragrunt instead.&lt;br&gt;[15] The BFF package and the templates are uploaded to the shared artifacts bucket (name read from SSM).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;Secret: AWS managed key, no rotation, TLS-only resource policy, public policies blocked, one reader role. The public client has no secret.&lt;br&gt;prod stacks (after B003): termination protection and a stack policy against replacing or deleting the pool, clients, secret, distribution and bucket. Until then prod is Terraform-owned and the owner guard stops a CloudFormation deploy there.&lt;br&gt;Solid arrow: request or deploy path. Dotted arrow: DNS, deploy-time value, alert or external call. Dashed box: owned outside this repository or prod only." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;verticalAlign=top;align=left;fontSize=15;fontColor=#232F3E;fontStyle=0;spacing=0;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1470" y="2200" width="1360" height="290" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>